{"kind": "local_or_unclassified_prose", "line": 13478, "review_required": true, "scope_stack": [], "text_excerpt": "We will say that $(U, A, f, M^\\bullet)$ is an {\\it affine chart} for $(X, D, M)$. Consider the ideals $I_i(M^\\bullet, f) \\subset A$ defined in More on Algebra, Section \\ref{more-algebra-section-perfect-eta}. Let us say $(X, S, M)$ is a {\\it good triple} if for every $x \\in D$ there exists an affine chart $(U, A, f, M^\\bullet)$ with $x \\in U$ and $I_i(M^\\bullet, f)$ principal ideals for all $i \\in \\mathbf{Z}$."}
